---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { toolCountLabel } from '../data/tools';

const seo = {
  title: 'Privacy Policy — Best Answer Hub',
  description: 'Privacy policy for Best Answer Hub. Learn how we collect, use, protect, and share your personal information. Compliant with GDPR, CCPA/CPRA, and COPPA.',
  url: '/privacy-policy/',
  type: 'WebPage' as const,
  breadcrumbs: [
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Privacy Policy', url: '/privacy-policy/' },
  ],
};
---

<LegalLayout seo={seo} title="Privacy Policy" lastUpdated="June 4, 2026">
  <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted mb-6">This Privacy Policy describes how Best Answer Hub ("we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, stores, and protects your personal information when you visit our website or purchase digital products. It applies to all visitors regardless of location and is designed to comply with the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), the California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA), and the Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA). For information specifically about cookies and tracking technologies, please see our <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>Information you provide voluntarily</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contact details</strong>: when you reach out via our contact form or email us directly.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Log data</strong>: IP address, browser type and version, pages visited, time spent on each page, referring URLs, and device type.</li>
    <li><strong>Device information</strong>: operating system, screen resolution, and browser language.</li>
    <li><strong>Cookies and similar technologies</strong>: see our <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> for a complete breakdown of categories, purposes, and retention periods.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Purchase and payment data</h3>
  <p>When you purchase a digital product through Best Answer Hub, your payment is processed by Paddle.com Market Limited, our Merchant of Record. We do not collect, store, or process your credit card number, bank account details, or other payment credentials. Paddle handles all payment data, billing, tax calculation, and invoicing as an independent data controller.</p>
  <p>Paddle may share the following transaction data with us for order fulfillment and customer support:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your email address (for delivery of digital products and receipt).</li>
    <li>Transaction ID, product purchased, and purchase date.</li>
    <li>Country of residence (for tax and compliance purposes).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>For details on how Paddle processes your payment data, see Paddle's <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/invoiced-consumer-terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Buyer Terms</a>.</p>

  <h3>What we do NOT collect</h3>
  <p>All free tools on Best Answer Hub (including the Mortgage Calculator, AI Cost Calculator, Image Compressor, PDF Converter, and {toolCountLabel} others) run entirely in your browser using client-side JavaScript. This means:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not see, store, or process any files you upload to our tools.</li>
    <li>We do not collect tool inputs, outputs, or usage data.</li>
    <li>We do not require accounts, passwords, or personal information to use any tool.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use your information</h2>
  <p>We use the information we collect for the following purposes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>To operate and maintain our website</strong>: ensuring pages load correctly and content is accessible.</li>
    <li><strong>To analyze traffic and improve our content</strong>: understanding which articles are helpful so we can produce better recommendations.</li>
    <li><strong>To track affiliate conversions</strong>: when you click partner links, we use tracking to attribute sales and earn commissions. See our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a> for details.</li>
    <li><strong>To fulfill digital product purchases</strong>: delivering purchased PDF reports and assessment results via email.</li>
    <li><strong>To comply with legal obligations</strong>: responding to lawful requests and maintaining records as required by law.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Affiliate links and data sharing</h2>
  <p>Our site contains affiliate links. When you click these links, the vendor may receive your click data (including approximate location, device type, and referral source) to attribute the conversion to us. If you make a purchase, we may earn a commission. This does not affect the price you pay.</p>
  <p>Under CCPA/CPRA, this data sharing for cross-context behavioral advertising may be considered "sharing" personal information. We provide a clear "Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information" mechanism through our cookie preference center and honor Global Privacy Control (GPC) signals automatically. See our <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> for opt-out instructions.</p>
  <p>We only recommend products we genuinely believe are useful. We do not sell your personal information to affiliate partners or any third party.</p>

  <h2>Third-party services and data recipients</h2>
  <p>We use trusted third-party services to operate our site and process transactions. These services may process data on our behalf:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Payment processor</strong>: Paddle.com Market Limited acts as our Merchant of Record for all transactions, handling payment processing, tax collection, invoicing, and refunds. Paddle is an independent data controller for payment data.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics providers</strong>: Google Analytics 4 (IP anonymization is enabled by default in GA4; data sharing with Google is disabled) to understand traffic patterns.</li>
    <li><strong>Hosting and CDN providers</strong>: Hostinger, for serving our website content securely and quickly.</li>
    <li><strong>Affiliate network platforms</strong>: Amazon Associates, CJ Affiliate, Impact, PartnerStack, and Awin, for conversion tracking.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We have agreements in place with these service providers that restrict their use of your data to the services they perform for us. We do not authorize them to use your data for their own marketing purposes.</p>

  <h2>Data retention</h2>
  <p>We retain personal information only for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes for which it was collected:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Analytics data</strong>: retained for up to 26 months, then aggregated and anonymized.</li>
    <li><strong>Contact form submissions</strong>: retained for 12 months unless you request deletion.</li>
    <li><strong>Affiliate conversion data</strong>: retained for the duration required by our partner agreements, typically 12–24 months.</li>
    <li><strong>Server logs</strong>: retained for 90 days for security and debugging, then deleted.</li>
    <li><strong>Purchase transaction records</strong>: retained for 7 years to comply with tax and accounting obligations. This includes order ID, product, date, and email address provided by Paddle.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cross-border data transfers</h2>
  <p>Our website is hosted on servers that may be located outside your country of residence. If you are in the EU/EEA, your data may be transferred to the United States or other countries. We ensure appropriate safeguards are in place, including Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) where required by GDPR, and we only work with service providers that maintain adequate data protection standards.</p>
  <p>Paddle processes payment data in accordance with its own data processing agreements and may transfer data internationally under Standard Contractual Clauses and other approved transfer mechanisms.</p>

  <h2>Your privacy rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on your location, you may have the following rights:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Right to access</strong>: request a copy of the personal information we hold about you.</li>
    <li><strong>Right to correction</strong>: request that we correct inaccurate or incomplete information.</li>
    <li><strong>Right to deletion</strong>: request that we delete your personal information, subject to legal retention requirements.</li>
    <li><strong>Right to restriction</strong>: request that we limit how we use your data.</li>
    <li><strong>Right to data portability</strong>: request a copy of your data in a structured, machine-readable format.</li>
    <li><strong>Right to object</strong>: object to processing based on legitimate interests or direct marketing.</li>
    <li><strong>Right to withdraw consent</strong>: withdraw consent for marketing or non-essential cookies at any time.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>For California residents specifically, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Know what categories of personal information we collect and how we use it.</li>
    <li>Opt out of the sale or sharing of your personal information through our <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> preference center or GPC signal.</li>
    <li>Request deletion of your personal information.</li>
    <li>Not be discriminated against for exercising your privacy rights.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To exercise any of these rights, contact us at <a href="mailto:admin@bestanswerhub.com">admin@bestanswerhub.com</a>. We will respond within 30 days and verify your identity before processing sensitive requests.</p>

  <h2>Data security</h2>
  <p>We implement industry-standard security measures to protect your data, including:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>HTTPS/TLS encryption for all data in transit.</li>
    <li>Secure hosting with regular security patches.</li>
    <li>Access controls and minimal data collection.</li>
    <li>Regular reviews of our service providers' security practices.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>While we take reasonable steps to protect your data, no method of transmission over the internet is 100% secure. If you believe your data has been compromised, please contact us immediately.</p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>Our website is not intended for children under 13 years of age. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you are a parent or guardian and believe we have inadvertently collected data from your child, please contact us at <a href="mailto:admin@bestanswerhub.com">admin@bestanswerhub.com</a> and we will delete the information promptly.</p>
  <p>Under COPPA, we do not target children, use child-directed marketing, or collect geolocation data from minors.</p>

  <h2>Global Privacy Control (GPC)</h2>
  <p>We honor the Global Privacy Control (GPC) signal sent by your browser. If you have GPC enabled, we automatically treat this as a valid opt-out request for the sale or sharing of personal information under CCPA/CPRA. No additional action is required from you. See our <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> for more details.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We review and update this Privacy Policy at least once per year, or sooner when regulations change or our data practices evolve. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page reflects the most recent revision. Material changes will be announced via a banner on our site for 30 days.</p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, want to exercise your data rights, or have a complaint, contact us at:</p>
  <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:admin@bestanswerhub.com">admin@bestanswerhub.com</a></p>
  <p><strong>Response time:</strong> We aim to respond to all privacy-related inquiries within 30 days.</p>
</LegalLayout>
